select round(AVG(LAT_N),4) 
FROM  (
select LAT_N,
row_number()over(order by LAT_N) as rownumber,
count(LAT_N)over() as total_rows
FROM station
) as t
where rownumber in (
    floor((total_rows+1)/2),
    ceil((total_rows+1)/2)
)
order by LAT_N asc


Explaination:
Concept	
ROW_NUMBER()	Gives each row a position
OVER()	Performs a calculation while keeping the rows
Subquery	Creates a temporary result to use outside
FLOOR()	Rounds down
CEIL()	Rounds up
IN	Checks whether something matches a list
AVG()	Calculates average
++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
Steps to solve
STATION
   ↓
Sort LAT_N
   ↓
ROW_NUMBER()
   ↓
Give every row a position
   ↓
COUNT()
   ↓
Find total number of rows
   ↓
FLOOR + CEIL
   ↓
Find middle position(s)
   ↓
WHERE + IN
   ↓
Keep middle value(s)
   ↓
AVG()
   ↓
Calculate median
   ↓
ROUND(..., 4)
   ↓
Final answer
